  "sport": "hockey",
  "title": "The M – diagonal pass and shot at speed",
  "description": "Two lines, one in each corner beside the net, with a cone on each side further out. The first in one line skates without the puck down and around their cone. The first in the other line plays a diagonal pass to the skater, who shoots first time near the cone. Then the passer skates around their cone and gets the pass from the other side, and so on. The skating paths make an M.\n\nSwap lines so everyone shoots from both sides, on the forehand and the backhand. A quick warm-up for both players and goalie. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Pass along the ice, to the blade."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "The skater shows with the stick where they want the puck."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Shoot first time – do not stop the puck first."
    }
  ],
